/** OPHELDU argument order. OpHeldUHandler resolves [opheldu,<obj>] on the FIRST pair before the
 *  second, so the TOOL always goes first: useItemOnItem(TOOL_obj, TOOL_slot, target_obj, target_slot).
 *  All four tools this file covers (knife, tinderbox, needle, ball_of_wool) have their own specific
 *  trigger, and each reads the target from last_useitem / last_useslot — so tool-first is correct for
 *  every one of them, and it also avoids the handler's fall-through branch, which swaps lastItem and
 *  lastUseItem UNCONDITIONALLY once the first lookup misses (OpHeldUHandler.ts:95-99).
 *  ONE EXCEPTION: achey_tree_logs has its own [opheldu,achey_tree_logs]; sending it FIRST reaches the
 *  dedicated achey firemaking script, sending the tinderbox first reaches the generic one. */
export const OPHELDU_TOOL_FIRST = true;

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT TO OBSERVE BETWEEN STEPS — the send is never the evidence
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The engine silently drops any packet it does not like (Component.get miss, wrong buttonType, a
// component whose rootLayer is not an open modal or tab, an inv slot that does not hold the obj you
// claimed, a script that is not suspended where you think it is). Every handler in that list just
// `return false`. So each step below names the SERVER-SIDE fact that proves it landed:
//
//   step                                  wait for
//   ------------------------------------  --------------------------------------------------------
//   opLoc(tree, 1)                        MESSAGES.woodcutting.swing, then a backpack +1 of the
//                                         product obj. NOT the send.
//   useItemOnItem(tinderbox, log)         MESSAGES.firemaking.attempt -> .success, then RE-READ
//                                         YOUR OWN TILE (the server moved you).
//   useItemOnItem(knife, log)             chatModalId === SKILL_MULTI_BY_NAME[iface].root
//   ifButton(make1|make5|make10)          fletching xp / product in the backpack; chatModalId -1
//   ifButton(makeX)                       P_COUNTDIALOG (leanbot sets countDialogTick), THEN
//                                         submitCountDialog(n). A reply sent before it is DROPPED.
//   useItemOnItem(needle, leather)        mainModalId === LEATHER_CRAFTING.ROOT. If it never opens,
//                                         suspect thread before you suspect the packet.
