// PACKET: opLoc(x, z, locId, 1) — ONE send. woodcut.rs2 re-arms itself with p_oploc(3) every cycle,
// so the server keeps swinging until the tree depletes, the backpack fills, or the player moves.
// NEVER send op 3 yourself: [oploc3,_tree] is the hidden continuation op.
// OPLOC self-routes NAIVELY (see learnings: naive-router rule) — stand on/next to the tree first.
// SUCCESS: a "You get some <log>." message AND a backpack +1 of the product obj. The tree usually
// survives several logs; on depletion the loc CHANGES to its next stage (loc_change), which the door
// tracker sees as LOC_ADD_CHANGE on that tile.
