// =================================================================================================
// FLETCHING — fletchLogs (+ bow stringing)
// =================================================================================================
// PACKET: useItemOnItem(KNIFE, knifeSlot, logObj, logSlot)
//   -> [opheldu,knife] (in skill_cooking/.../cutting_fruit.rs2, NOT in skill_fletching) whose default
//      arm forwards category_22 to @fletch_log. cut_logs.rs2's own [opheldu,_category_22] 'case knife'
//      is DEAD CODE — OpHeldUHandler resolves obj-specific triggers before category triggers.
//   -> the server if_openchat's skill_multi3 for plain logs (15 shafts / short / long) or skill_multi2
//      for every other log (short / long). Read chatModalId to tell which.
//   -> ifButton(SKILL_MULTI[iface].slots[i].make1|make5|make10) to commit; or makeX then, once
//      P_COUNTDIALOG lands, submitCountDialog(n).
// ⛔ THESE ARE RESUME BUTTONS. IF_BUTTON on the component is the ONLY accepted answer — the plain
//   dialog-continue path (RESUME_PAUSEBUTTON) is explicitly refused while a choice is pending.
// ⛔ MEMBERS GATE. @fletch_log opens with `if (map_members = ^false) { mes(^mes_members_fletching); return; }`
//   so on an F2P world the dialog NEVER OPENS. The engine default is members:true (WorldConfig.ts:100,
//   overridable by NODE_MEMBERS) — verify on the target server before trusting this path.
// PRODUCTION RATE: one product every 2 ticks, driven by a server weakqueue; it stops early with
//   "You have run out of <log>."
