//      more often than it means "the packet was dropped".
//   -> ifButton(LEATHER_PRODUCTS[i].buttons[1|5|10]). @craft_leather starts with if_close, so a
//      successful click closes the modal — IF_CLOSE is the acknowledgement.
// These ARE ordinary [if_button,...] triggers (unlike skill_multiN), so no resume-button bookkeeping.
// hard_leather and dragonhide DO NOT use this interface — see HARD_LEATHER and DHIDE below.
// THREAD: one reel is consumed per 5 products (%thread_used > 4); the counter is a player var that
// persists across sessions, so the first reel of a session may go after fewer than 5.
// PRODUCTION RATE: one product every 2 ticks via a server weakqueue.
